-- title:
--   Completion of a cyclic cover of a thickness-n crossing
-- statement:
--   Let $W$ be a complete discrete valuation ring (a Noetherian local domain that is a discrete valuation ring, adically complete for its maximal ideal), let $\pi \in W$ be irreducible, let $n$ be a positive natural number whose image in $W$ is a unit, and assume $W$ contains a primitive $n$-th root of unity. Let $S^\flat$ and $S$ be Noetherian local rings with $S$ an integrally closed domain, $S$ an $S^\flat$-algebra that is finite as a module with injective structure map, $\operatorname{ringKrullDim} S \le 2$ and $2 \le \operatorname{ringKrullDim} S$, and $2 \le \operatorname{ringKrullDim} S^\flat$. Let $t$ be a non-zero element of the maximal ideal of $S$. Assume: $S$ is unramified over $S^\flat$ at every prime of $S$ that is not maximal; every element of $S$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $S$ to an element coming from $S^\flat$; and there is a ring isomorphism $e^\flat$ from the maximal-adic completion of $S^\flat$ onto $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ (\pi^n)$, that is, onto $W[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi^n)$ (formally, the quotient of $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}\ (\mathrm{Fin}\ 2)\ W$ by the ideal generated by $X_0X_1 - C(\pi^n)$). Let $K_1$ be a fraction field of $S^\flat$ and $K$ a fraction field of $S$, arranged in compatible towers $S^\flat \to S \to K$ and $S^\flat \to K_1 \to K$, with $K/K_1$ finite Galois with cyclic Galois group $K \simeq_{\mathrm{alg}[K_1]} K$ and $[K:K_1] = n$. Then there is a ring isomorphism $e$ from the maximal-adic completion of $S$ onto $\mathrm{UVCrossingModel}\ W\ \pi = W[[U,V]]/(UV - \pi)$ which is compatible with constants read through $e^\flat$: for all $x \in S^\flat$ and $w \in W$, if $e^\flat$ sends the image of $x$ in the completion of $S^\flat$ to the class $\mathrm{const}\ (\pi^n)\ w$ of the constant power series $C(w)$, then $e$ sends the image of $x$ in the completion of $S$ to the class $\mathrm{const}\ \pi\ w$ of $C(w)$.
--
--   This is the completed form of a Kummer-type descent: a degree-$n$ cyclic cover, unramified away from the closed point and with trivial residue extension, of a complete local ring isomorphic to a crossing of thickness $n$ is itself a crossing of thickness one, compatibly with the $W$-constants. It is used in the analysis of the local structure of the stable model of $X_1(Mp)$ at a supersingular point, where the thickness-$n$ floor is the $\Gamma_0(p)$-level ring and the cyclic cover is the diamond cover; it is cited by the corresponding statement about the completed stalk on $X_1(Mp)$ at tame level.
